<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mythen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Grosser Mythen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mythen are a pair of limestone peaks above the town of Schwyz in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>: the Grosser Mythen, 1,898 metres high, and the Kleiner Mythen. Their distinctive shape dominates the valley of Schwyz and has long served as a landmark of the region where the Swiss Confederacy began.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mythen.jpg" alt="Mythen" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hannes Röst · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mythen_Panorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
